\\cdot \\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d084334-b89a-5a33-9373-086018cdfbc3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Factorial of Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f466c3d-5864-5b6f-ad2f-aa96d92c1b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277750} {:answer/id #uuid "ba74b5c5-f2e7-55f2-ae66-9d09a24da10b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277751} {:answer/id #uuid "afe5714f-2298-59c4-a4cd-ffd6087f2e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277752} {:answer/id #uuid "8b29827a-802a-570f-9f5c-7a9f3d5f8bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277753} {:answer/id #uuid "af7faa30-db6b-529b-a87c-67af05d5155d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe5714f-2298-59c4-a4cd-ffd6087f2e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277752} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f6eac6-8436-568a-b1ab-e6cd5a08bb09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f64c95d-acbb-53bc-85d8-79327c4ad48e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124393" :question/problem "$5!\\,0!=$" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is a product of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $5!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n5!=5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=120.\n$$\n\n- By definition, the factorial of zero equals one:\n\n$$\n0!=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5!\\,0! & =120\\cdot 1=120\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d084334-b89a-5a33-9373-086018cdfbc3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Factorial of Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4a77783-9262-5057-90f6-7e1c72edcbfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "119" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277757} {:answer/id #uuid "46652e7d-a8fb-5edc-ac11-54326a678109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277758} {:answer/id #uuid "2e8b041c-fa5f-514c-aa74-aca4c1d8f02e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277759} {:answer/id #uuid "e336ea18-2d07-55c8-8211-90820eb60631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277760} {:answer/id #uuid "76425271-aecb-5472-a7a7-adb138ed4c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4a77783-9262-5057-90f6-7e1c72edcbfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "119" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277757} :answer-field/id #uuid "62b9bb1f-31cb-5baf-aa54-0af64faa028a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4c5aade-a9e1-5acb-a869-03c1f74922e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-124405" :question/problem "$5!-0!=$" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is a subtraction of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $5!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n5!=5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=120.\n$$\n\n- By definition, the factorial of zero equals one:\n\n$$\n0!=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5!-0! & =120-1=119\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277762 :knowledge-point